<article class="env-lemma" id="0AV6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AV6">Lemma <span data-tag="0AV6">15.24.11</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $M$, $N$ be finite $R$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $N$ has property $(S_1)$, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, N)$ has property $(S_1)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $N$ has property $(S_2)$, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, N)$ has property $(S_2)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $R$ is a domain, $N$ is torsion free and $(S_2)$, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, N)$ is torsion free and has property $(S_2)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since localizing at primes commutes with taking $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R$ for finite $R$-modules (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/08YR" data-tag="08YR">10.71.9</a>) parts (1) and (2) follow immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AV5" data-tag="0AV5">15.24.10</a>. Part (3) follows from (2) and Lemma <a href="/tag/0AUX" data-tag="0AUX">15.22.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>